SRC/ogrify -- ogrify, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================ogrify folds text to lower case, drops its punctuation, wraps it to40 columns, and replaces words at random -- five in a hundred bydefault -- with words from a word list.  ogre.words is the list it wasposted with, words in the manner of industrial-music lyrics.  Version2.0, `by Morpheus', 13 March 1992, a rewrite of an ogrify first postedto rec.music.industrial.  From the `silly' collection posted toalt.sources in December 1992.ORIG holds ogrify.c and ogre.words as posted.ogrify.c and ogre.words are unchanged; ogre.words here is CR-terminated,as every text file on this disk is.  rand() is linked from/dd/LIB/rand.r.The word list must be named on the command line.  Without one, ogrifysays `ogrify: unable to open ""' and stops.    echo "the quick brown fox" | ogrify ogre.words -50    ogrify -h